Z||000000||Fiero*101||11-17-2001||01:46 AM||||Well i got my car back today from getting the new exhaust put on it. and my mechanic tells me my Manifolds are leaking thats why they glow. and thats why even though i have an exhaust system on it it is still a little to loud.<BR>Ok i have a few ?'s<BR>How do i fix this problem w/ out getting new?<BR>and if i do have to get new how much are we talking?<BR>and If i do need new and i get new ones how do i put them on? Dont i need to drop the engine to put on the manifold in the back ?<P>Just a few ?'s im pondering in my head.<BR>Any info right now is GREAT INFO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fiero*101<BR>Gold 86 SE 2M6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar101.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mickey_Moose||11-17-2001||10:01 AM||||No you don't have to drop the engine, can be taken out mostly by undoing the bolts that are holding them on - do a search here, lots of info.<P>As for them leaking...could be several things, bad gasket, broken bolt, cracked manifold (can be fixed)...<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||revin||11-17-2001||10:10 AM||||How about a clogged cat.! or muffler? THAT is probably how you got a crack in the manifold. Price? start saving! but not so bad!<BR>check in to it!||||reg||1
